DefenseClaw for Windows
https://github.com/Rmontalbano/defenseclaw_win

A community Windows companion app for Cisco DefenseClaw
(https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/defenseclaw). It is not an official
Cisco product. Cisco and DefenseClaw are trademarks of Cisco Systems, Inc.
and/or its affiliates.

This product includes work adapted from the following projects, both
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  DefenseClaw for macOS
  https://github.com/keitheobrien/defenseclaw_mac
    Several features follow that app's design and behaviour, and some logic
    was translated from Swift to C#, including the structured audit-detail
    parser, the Overview attention rules and doctor reconciliation, the
    inspector layout policy, connector onboarding, and egress decoding. The
    Policies panel for a runtime with the policy model follows that app's
    design: scopes with inherited values, tool-call levels kept apart from
    LLM thresholds, an acknowledgement for a change that protects less, and
    a rule pack that must validate before it is switched to.

  DefenseClaw
  https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/defenseclaw
    Some input validation and display-redaction patterns mirror the
    DefenseClaw CLI so the app accepts and hides exactly what the CLI does.
    The command palette's command catalogue is generated from DefenseClaw's
    TUI command registry (tui/registry_data.py: names, arguments and
    descriptions of its commands, and each runtime's Windows platform table),
    by tools/gen-tui-registry.py.
    The Policies model (how a scope's levels are resolved, what each view
    lists, what counts as a weaker setting, and the wording of what each
    change does) is translated from the runtime's own Python policy model
    and TUI panel (defenseclaw.tui.services.policy_state, policy_catalog and
    policy_panel), so the app states the same facts the runtime does.

The changes are this project's own: the code is a separate C#/WPF
implementation for Windows.
